# **Sovereign OS — Complete System Architecture and In-Depth Overview**

## **1. What Sovereign OS is designed to become**

**Sovereign OS is a bootable, declarative, federated, cognitive operating system built on NixOS.** It is designed to bring together computing infrastructure, artificial intelligence, specialized workspaces, autonomous agents, services, data, automation, governance, and physical systems under one unified operating environment.

The important distinction is that Sovereign OS is not intended to be just another Linux distribution, an AI assistant, a Kubernetes cluster, or a collection of applications.

It is intended to be the system that coordinates all of those things.

Sovereign owns the operational authority, identity, governance, policy, orchestration, lifecycle, memory, planning, scheduling, model routing, and execution coordination of the federation.

NixOS provides the declarative operating-system foundation. Federation Core provides the central coordination and governance mechanisms. The 16 Domain Workspaces provide specialized capabilities. The runtime executes and manages the system's workloads. Models and agents provide intelligence. Hardware provides the resources.

The overall objective is to create an operating system capable of coordinating a distributed ecosystem of computers, services, models, agents, applications, workspaces, databases, automation systems, and eventually robotics.

